<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY BANK SALE DECISION NOT PUBLIC YET - OFFICIAL.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY BANK SALE DECISION NOT PUBLIC YET - OFFICIAL.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's state privatisation agency APV Rt selected the winning tender on Thursday for the sale of Magyar Hitel Bank (MHB) but will let the Finance Ministry make the announcement, an APV official said.</p>
<p>Arpad Kovacs, president of APV, said the agency's board selected the winner, identified by sources as Dutch bank ABN AMRO NV , but could not announce it because the Finance Ministry has ownership rights.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry is expected to hold a news conference on Friday to announce the winning tender to buy Hungary's fifth largest bank. -- Budapest newsroom ++36 1 327 4040</p>
